.TH LIONCTL-SESSION 1 "2026-10-03" "LionOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lionctl session \- admin subcommand for lion-session (spec 02 §9)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lionctl session
.IR command " [" argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Operates the LionOS session supervisor through its D\-Bus service
.BR os.lionos.Session1 .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print State, InhibitedActions, SafeMode and current Blockers.
.TP
.B lock
Lock the session (logind LockSession/LockSessions).
.TP
.B logout
Request a graceful logout (query apps, respect inhibitors).
.TP
.B restart \fR|\fP shutdown \fR|\fP suspend \fR|\fP hibernate
Lifecycle actions through logind.
.TP
.B switch\-user
Lock all sessions and hand the seat to the greeter.
.TP
.B inhibit \fIWHAT\fP \fIWHO\fP \fIWHY\fP
Hold an inhibitor (logout/shutdown/suspend/idle/switch\-user) until
Ctrl\-C.
.TP
.B register \fIAPP_ID\fP
Register as an end\-session client; acknowledges queries after 1 s.
.TP
.B signals
Print SessionReady / QueryEndSession / EndSession / ServiceFailed as
they arrive.
.TP
.BR check " / " version " / " schema
\-\-check\-config / \-\-version / \-\-print\-schema of the daemon binary.
.TP
.BR start " / " stop " / " restart " / " reload
systemctl \-\-user verbs for lion\-session.service (reload sends SIGHUP).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lionctl session status
lionctl session inhibit shutdown lion\-updates "installing updates"
lionctl session logout
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lion\-session (8)
